1
00:00:25,826 --> 00:00:28,026
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:38,203
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:52,317
♪ ♪

4
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,233
♪ ♪

5
00:01:39,199 --> 00:01:40,999
♪ ♪

6
00:02:14,601 --> 00:02:16,534
♪ ♪

7
00:02:24,645 --> 00:02:27,946
So, Mr. Beloit, you would
like this court to believe

8
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:31,583
that your brother, the
defendant, Tom Beloit,

9
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:34,285
could not have
killed his wife's lover

10
00:02:34,355 --> 00:02:36,688
because he was
with you that night.

11
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:38,037
That's right.

12
00:02:38,092 --> 00:02:39,757
Uh-huh.

13
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:43,027
Who drove to the bar you
allegedly went to that night,

14
00:02:43,097 --> 00:02:44,463
you or your brother?

15
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:46,498
What do you mean, "allegedly"?

16
00:02:46,567 --> 00:02:47,732
Huh?

17
00:02:47,801 --> 00:02:49,066
We were there.

18
00:02:49,136 --> 00:02:51,503
Just answer the question,
please, Mr. Beloit.

19
00:02:51,572 --> 00:02:53,805
I drove.

20
00:02:53,874 --> 00:02:56,474
And whose car did you
drive, yours or your brother's?

21
00:02:56,544 --> 00:02:58,076
Mine. Look...

22
00:02:58,145 --> 00:03:00,746
I already told the cops.

23
00:03:00,814 --> 00:03:02,514
Tom and I drove to the Cedar Bar

24
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:04,816
to check out a
singer for our club.

25
00:03:04,885 --> 00:03:06,617
We got there around 10:00.

26
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:10,489
We left around 11:00,
after she finished her set.

27
00:03:10,557 --> 00:03:14,359
And then you drove home
in your car, is that correct?

28
00:03:14,428 --> 00:03:16,527
Yes.

29
00:03:16,597 --> 00:03:19,731
But you can't identify
one single person

30
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,400
who saw you there
that night, can you?

31
00:03:22,469 --> 00:03:24,402
It was Friday night!

32
00:03:25,506 --> 00:03:27,639
The place was jammed.

33
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,607
But we were there.

34
00:03:29,677 --> 00:03:31,843
And your car was
there, too, right?

35
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:33,845
How many times I have to say it?

36
00:03:33,914 --> 00:03:38,417
Mr. Beloit, are you aware
that perjury is a crime

37
00:03:38,485 --> 00:03:41,119
for which there are
severe penalties?

38
00:03:41,188 --> 00:03:42,987
I'm telling the truth.

39
00:03:45,826 --> 00:03:48,893
You own a bar, Mr. Beloit.

40
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:54,465
Is it true what they say,
that customers come in

41
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:56,468
and tell you their troubles?

42
00:03:58,372 --> 00:04:00,305
Yeah. Yeah, that's true.

43
00:04:00,374 --> 00:04:03,040
And sometimes you tell them
your troubles, too, don't you?

44
00:04:03,109 --> 00:04:06,411
I talked to some of the
customers at your bar,

45
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,846
and according to them,
you complain that your car

46
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:11,115
is always in the
shop... Is that true?

47
00:04:13,387 --> 00:04:15,319
I got a lemon.

48
00:04:15,389 --> 00:04:19,691
And that's where your car
was on the night of the murder...

49
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,393
In the shop.

50
00:04:23,163 --> 00:04:26,131
I have a copy of the
work order right here.

51
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:28,378
Uh... uh...

52
00:04:28,402 --> 00:04:30,869
Don't... do it, Mr. Beloit.

53
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,972
Don't get yourself in deeper.

54
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:36,408
You didn't go anywhere
with your brother that night.

55
00:04:36,476 --> 00:04:39,277
You weren't even with your
brother that night, were you?

56
00:04:39,346 --> 00:04:40,578
Yes...

57
00:04:40,647 --> 00:04:43,515
you love your brother,
and you want to help him.

58
00:04:43,584 --> 00:04:46,952
And we can understand
that, but you must not lie

59
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:49,287
for him.

60
00:04:49,356 --> 00:04:52,990
He wasn't with you that night...

61
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:57,895
because that night,
he was, in fact...

62
00:04:57,964 --> 00:05:00,231
murdering his wife's lover.

63
00:05:03,536 --> 00:05:05,470
Ladies and
gentlemen of the jury,

64
00:05:05,538 --> 00:05:07,138
have you reached a verdict?

65
00:05:08,242 --> 00:05:10,141
Yes, we have, Your Honor.

66
00:05:11,245 --> 00:05:13,078
The defendant will please rise.

67
00:05:17,251 --> 00:05:19,062
May we have your
verdict, please?

68
00:05:19,086 --> 00:05:22,320
We, the jury, find the
defendant, Thomas Beloit,

69
00:05:22,388 --> 00:05:24,822
guilty of murder
in the first degree.

70
00:05:30,196 --> 00:05:32,163
Tommy... Tommy...

71
00:05:32,232 --> 00:05:33,865
Tommy, don't worry.

72
00:05:33,934 --> 00:05:35,712
Ms. March! Ms. March!
JULIE: Thank you.

73
00:05:35,736 --> 00:05:38,180
Not right now. Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
Excuse us. Coming through. Excuse us.

74
00:05:38,204 --> 00:05:39,849
Congratulations. Hey, thanks!

75
00:05:40,874 --> 00:05:41,807
I know!

76
00:05:41,875 --> 00:05:43,842
Julie? Julie?

77
00:05:43,911 --> 00:05:46,244
Mike Eiseman.

78
00:05:46,313 --> 00:05:49,647
What brings you to Atlanta?

79
00:05:49,717 --> 00:05:51,482
I'm just passing through.

80
00:05:51,551 --> 00:05:53,585
Um, well, I'm on
vacation, sort of.

81
00:05:53,653 --> 00:05:56,087
My mother's down in
Florida visiting her sister,

82
00:05:56,156 --> 00:05:58,123
so she wants me to drive
down and bring her back,

83
00:05:58,192 --> 00:05:59,658
so I thought I would stop,

84
00:05:59,726 --> 00:06:02,960
uh, on the way to... see you.

85
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:05,830
Well, Atlanta isn't
exactly on your way.

86
00:06:05,899 --> 00:06:07,765
Oh, Mike,

87
00:06:07,835 --> 00:06:09,967
this is Eli Boward, an
attorney in my office.

88
00:06:10,037 --> 00:06:11,881
Mike Eiseman, an
old friend of mine.

89
00:06:11,905 --> 00:06:12,837
Hi.

90
00:06:12,906 --> 00:06:14,339
Um, listen, you wouldn't, uh,

91
00:06:14,408 --> 00:06:17,241
by any chance be free
for, you know, lunch, or...?

92
00:06:17,311 --> 00:06:18,943
Well...

93
00:06:19,012 --> 00:06:20,545
Uh, gee, Mike,

94
00:06:20,614 --> 00:06:23,348
I'm sorry, uh, Julie and I
are having a working lunch.

95
00:06:23,417 --> 00:06:25,716
We've just been assigned
to the Branca case.

96
00:06:25,786 --> 00:06:28,186
Oh, Mike, I'm sorry.

97
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:29,988
No, oh, you know, I mean,

98
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:31,668
you know, I mean, I
should have called and...

99
00:06:31,692 --> 00:06:33,236
But let's talk before
you go, okay?

100
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,626
Where are you staying?

101
00:06:34,695 --> 00:06:36,828
Um, the Grand Hotel.

102
00:06:36,897 --> 00:06:38,095
Bye.

103
00:06:38,165 --> 00:06:39,330
Grand. Bye.

104
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,998
Bye.

105
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,545
Branca case! Mm-hmm.

106
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:46,409
You just convicted
an innocent man, lady!

107
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:49,586
You just convicted an innocent
man. A jury of his peers convicted...

108
00:06:49,610 --> 00:06:50,820
No, you! You did it!

109
00:06:50,844 --> 00:06:52,087
You did it! The jury
believed your lie!

110
00:06:52,111 --> 00:06:53,390
Okay, okay, hey,
hey, hold it. Hey! Hey!

111
00:06:53,414 --> 00:06:54,612
Hey!

112
00:06:56,883 --> 00:06:58,728
Nobody railroads my
brother and gets away with it.

113
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,485
Mr. Beloit, I know you're upset.

114
00:07:02,189 --> 00:07:03,488
What's going on?

115
00:07:03,557 --> 00:07:06,117
I'm gonna get you for this!

116
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,070
What is he talking
about... "get you"?

117
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,905
Oh, he's just...
Are-Are you all right?

118
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,707
I'm fine, I'm fine. Hi, Eli. Hi.

119
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:12,964
You don't look all right.

120
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:14,933
It's all right; I'm okay.

121
00:07:15,002 --> 00:07:17,668
Did... Did-Did that
guy threaten you?

122
00:07:17,737 --> 00:07:19,682
His brother was just
convicted of murder,

123
00:07:19,706 --> 00:07:21,139
so he's kind of upset.

124
00:07:21,208 --> 00:07:22,707
Oh, that's right, your case.

125
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:24,042
Congratulations.

126
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,110
Thank you.

127
00:07:25,179 --> 00:07:27,011
If-If that guy threatened you,

128
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,681
don't you think you
should file a report?

129
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:32,117
No, no, he was just
blowing off steam.

130
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:00,545
Hello?

131
00:08:00,614 --> 00:08:01,813
Hello?

132
00:08:25,038 --> 00:08:27,605
Hello?

133
00:08:27,674 --> 00:08:29,674
Who is this?

134
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,699
Hello?

135
00:09:28,768 --> 00:09:31,702
Hello, Julie. It's me.

136
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,220
Who are you, and why are you

137
00:10:56,289 --> 00:10:57,722
following...

138
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:29,821
It's white tablet paper,
black permanent marker.

139
00:11:29,889 --> 00:11:31,867
You can buy them
in any grocery store.

140
00:11:31,891 --> 00:11:33,558
I'll send it over to the lab,

141
00:11:33,627 --> 00:11:35,760
but I doubt that
they'll find prints.

142
00:11:35,829 --> 00:11:38,863
There's not much we can
do in a situation like this.

143
00:11:38,932 --> 00:11:42,066
Bob, the man was in my garage.

144
00:11:42,135 --> 00:11:44,769
And-And he called me
so many times last night,

145
00:11:44,838 --> 00:11:46,415
I had to disconnect the phone.

146
00:11:46,439 --> 00:11:49,373
Well, Julie, I need
proof that it's Nick Beloit.

147
00:11:49,442 --> 00:11:52,844
He threatened me
in front of witnesses.

148
00:11:52,912 --> 00:11:54,779
Threats aren't proof of a crime.

149
00:11:54,848 --> 00:11:56,525
You, of all people, know that.

150
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:59,183
Look, let me work
on the note. Uh,

151
00:11:59,252 --> 00:12:01,385
if there's anything
there, I'll be all over him.

152
00:12:01,454 --> 00:12:05,056
Uh, Julie... I'm sorry.

153
00:12:05,125 --> 00:12:06,368
Yes, yes.

154
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:09,160
We all know the law.

155
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:12,630
But the man has my phone number.

156
00:12:12,698 --> 00:12:15,258
And he knows where I live.

157
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:19,337
I don't know what to do.

158
00:12:22,108 --> 00:12:23,868
I'll...

159
00:12:24,877 --> 00:12:26,945
I'll put Conrad on it.

160
00:12:27,013 --> 00:12:30,014
If this Nick Beloit
harasses you again,

161
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:31,093
we'll get him.

162
00:12:31,117 --> 00:12:32,716
Okay?

163
00:12:32,785 --> 00:12:35,486
Um... uh, uh,

164
00:12:35,555 --> 00:12:39,624
m-meantime, w-what
would you think of...

165
00:12:39,693 --> 00:12:41,526
staying with me?

166
00:12:41,595 --> 00:12:44,095
Oh, okay with me.

167
00:12:44,163 --> 00:12:45,396
All right.

168
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:48,132
That'd take care of the
mysterious phone calls

169
00:12:48,201 --> 00:12:50,201
and anonymous notes.

170
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:51,335
Did you sleep any?

171
00:12:51,404 --> 00:12:53,049
Not a wink. Oh.

172
00:12:53,073 --> 00:12:56,007
Well... Well, let's...
let's go pack a bag.

173
00:12:57,410 --> 00:12:59,010
No.

174
00:12:59,079 --> 00:13:00,878
What? No.

175
00:13:00,947 --> 00:13:02,880
I can't do it. Well...

176
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:05,950
I'm not going to give
him the satisfaction

177
00:13:06,019 --> 00:13:08,853
of driving me out
of my own home.

178
00:13:08,921 --> 00:13:10,221
At least, not yet.

179
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:12,556
Let's... Let's give it

180
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:16,560
another 24 hours, and
maybe he'll go away.

181
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:19,074
Do you think that's wise?

182
00:13:19,098 --> 00:13:21,032
I don't know.

183
00:14:23,997 --> 00:14:25,462
Hello?

184
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:28,466
You look lovely in blue.

185
00:14:34,407 --> 00:14:38,876
If you think you're
frightening me, Mr. Beloit,

186
00:14:38,945 --> 00:14:40,645
you're wrong.

187
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:42,547
And if you keep this up,

188
00:14:42,615 --> 00:14:45,149
sooner or later, you're
going to make a mistake,

189
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:47,029
and that's when
I'm going to nail you.

190
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:49,386
And then you are going to
join your brother in prison.

191
00:14:49,456 --> 00:14:50,688
And now the show is over.

192
00:15:14,681 --> 00:15:16,225
You all right? I'm all right.

193
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:18,048
I just panicked. I'm sorry.

194
00:15:18,117 --> 00:15:19,784
Oh, don't be sorry.

195
00:15:19,853 --> 00:15:22,413
Somebody peeping in your window.

196
00:15:23,122 --> 00:15:25,167
Must be in that high-rise
across the street.

197
00:15:25,191 --> 00:15:26,191
Yeah.

198
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:28,136
Conrad will be
there. You packed?

199
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,880
Almost. Okay.

200
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:33,530
Ben, I've given this a
great deal of thought.

201
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:35,833
I'm going to stay at your house,

202
00:15:35,902 --> 00:15:37,947
but I'm going to go
to work in the morning.

203
00:15:37,971 --> 00:15:38,903
Julie!

204
00:15:38,972 --> 00:15:40,938
I am going to do my job.

205
00:15:41,007 --> 00:15:43,285
I am not going to
let this disrupt my life.

206
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:45,243
Well, c-couldn't you
take a few days off?

207
00:15:45,311 --> 00:15:46,343
No.

208
00:15:46,412 --> 00:15:47,923
Well, what-what,
what-what... I know...

209
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,514
Wh-what if you leave
your work clothes here?

210
00:15:52,085 --> 00:15:54,152
Let's go.

211
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:56,154
Well, I'll take the bag.

212
00:16:21,347 --> 00:16:22,627
Good morning.

213
00:16:22,682 --> 00:16:24,448
Oh, good morning. Hey.

214
00:16:24,517 --> 00:16:25,583
Did you sleep?

215
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:26,995
Yes. Good.

216
00:16:27,019 --> 00:16:28,430
At first, I didn't
think I would,

217
00:16:28,454 --> 00:16:30,265
and then, all of a
sudden, it was morning.

218
00:16:31,557 --> 00:16:32,956
Phone didn't ring once.

219
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:34,570
Maybe he got
tired and it's over.

220
00:16:34,594 --> 00:16:36,159
Yeah.

221
00:16:36,228 --> 00:16:37,862
This will be ready in a minute.

222
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:41,432
Oh... I don't eat breakfast.

223
00:16:41,501 --> 00:16:42,933
You have to eat breakfast.

224
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,835
It's the most important
meal of the day.

225
00:16:44,904 --> 00:16:46,081
You sound like my mother.

226
00:16:47,473 --> 00:16:49,754
Well, you can bet your sweet
patootie I'm not your mother.

227
00:16:50,777 --> 00:16:52,175
But you got to eat breakfast.

228
00:16:52,244 --> 00:16:54,879
Oh, Ben, Eli and I

229
00:16:54,947 --> 00:16:56,380
have the Branca case.

230
00:16:56,449 --> 00:16:58,093
Yeah? Yeah, yeah.

231
00:16:58,117 --> 00:17:00,684
And we blocked out the
whole day to work on it together.

232
00:17:00,753 --> 00:17:02,286
Yeah, yeah.

233
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:04,900
So I, uh, guess I better go.

234
00:17:04,924 --> 00:17:06,356
Well, wait a minute... uh...

235
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:11,629
Here.

236
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:13,598
There.

237
00:17:13,666 --> 00:17:15,332
Egg sandwich.

238
00:17:15,401 --> 00:17:17,668
If you starve to death,
it won't be my fault.

239
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:20,478
Thank you. Yeah.

240
00:17:33,286 --> 00:17:35,186
Hello?

241
00:17:35,254 --> 00:17:36,387
Anybody there?

242
00:17:36,455 --> 00:17:37,721
Hello!

243
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:40,491
This is the only apartment
on this side of the building...

244
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,859
that's been rented
in the last month?

245
00:17:42,928 --> 00:17:44,861
Yeah, the last <i>six</i> months.

246
00:17:51,237 --> 00:17:52,503
Guess she hasn't moved in yet.

247
00:17:54,273 --> 00:17:55,273
She?

248
00:17:55,341 --> 00:17:56,273
Yeah.

249
00:17:56,342 --> 00:17:57,541
Rented it to a woman.

250
00:17:57,610 --> 00:17:59,543
Name's, um...

251
00:17:59,612 --> 00:18:01,345
Lisa Johnson.

252
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:02,546
Mannish kind of dame.

253
00:18:02,615 --> 00:18:05,716
Tall, dark hair, about
down to her shoulders,

254
00:18:05,785 --> 00:18:07,151
plain dress, below the knee.

255
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,252
Didn't talk much.

256
00:18:08,321 --> 00:18:10,521
Had kind of a low voice,
you know what I mean?

257
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:12,556
Yeah.

258
00:18:14,327 --> 00:18:15,971
Anyway, the name's Lisa Johnson.

259
00:18:15,995 --> 00:18:18,474
At least that's the
name she gave me.

260
00:18:18,498 --> 00:18:20,809
Paid me in cash, so I
didn't ask any questions.

261
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:23,111
"Never look a gift horse
in the mouth," I always say.

262
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:24,375
You know what I mean? Yeah.

263
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:30,707
When did she rent it?

264
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,109
Last Tuesday.

265
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,586
Phone works.

266
00:18:44,691 --> 00:18:48,226
You have her former address,
her work number, anything?

267
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,160
She paid cash.

268
00:18:52,231 --> 00:18:53,231
Okay.

269
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,483
Okay.

270
00:19:12,552 --> 00:19:15,486
If you hear from Lisa Johnson,

271
00:19:15,555 --> 00:19:16,987
you give me a call.

272
00:19:30,436 --> 00:19:31,869
A man of principle.

273
00:19:31,937 --> 00:19:33,871
Yeah.

274
00:19:43,882 --> 00:19:46,216
Come in.

275
00:19:46,285 --> 00:19:47,985
Oh, hi, Eli.

276
00:19:48,054 --> 00:19:49,153
Are you all right?

277
00:19:49,221 --> 00:19:50,587
Fine.

278
00:19:50,656 --> 00:19:53,023
Is something wrong?

279
00:19:53,092 --> 00:19:56,726
Well, um... you were
due in court at 10:30.

280
00:19:56,795 --> 00:19:57,895
Motions... the Branca case.

281
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:00,698
Oh, I'm sorry.

282
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:02,310
Oh, no, no, it's all
right. I took care of it.

283
00:20:02,334 --> 00:20:04,902
How could I have done that?

284
00:20:04,971 --> 00:20:06,670
It's right here in my calendar.

285
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:09,072
How could I just forget?

286
00:20:11,177 --> 00:20:14,044
Julie, look, why don't
you take some time off,

287
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:15,379
get away for a while.

288
00:20:15,448 --> 00:20:19,183
Now, Paula and I have
a place in the country,

289
00:20:19,252 --> 00:20:21,385
up near Jasper, and
you are welcome to it.

290
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:24,855
Oh, thanks, Eli, but
I need to stay here.

291
00:20:24,923 --> 00:20:28,326
At work, I feel like I
have some sort of control.

292
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:29,760
Mm-hmm.

293
00:20:29,828 --> 00:20:31,028
I mean, I did.

294
00:20:32,598 --> 00:20:35,799
I won't forget anything
again, I promise.

295
00:20:35,868 --> 00:20:36,800
Okay.

296
00:20:36,869 --> 00:20:38,335
But you remember,

297
00:20:38,404 --> 00:20:41,105
any time you want to
use the place, it's all right.

298
00:20:41,173 --> 00:20:42,306
And Paula says so, too.

299
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:43,375
Thanks.

300
00:20:53,786 --> 00:20:56,954
Hello. Who is this?

301
00:20:57,023 --> 00:20:57,955
Well, yes, it is.

302
00:20:58,024 --> 00:20:59,523
Who is this?

303
00:21:00,626 --> 00:21:01,925
Oh, um...

304
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:03,894
Well, just a minute, uh...

305
00:21:03,963 --> 00:21:05,763
Michael Eiseman.

306
00:21:10,837 --> 00:21:12,136
Hi.

307
00:21:12,205 --> 00:21:15,306
Are you still in town?

308
00:21:15,374 --> 00:21:16,273
Oh...

309
00:21:16,342 --> 00:21:20,077
no, tonight's not very good.

310
00:21:20,146 --> 00:21:23,013
Uh, tomorrow...

311
00:21:23,082 --> 00:21:25,182
Uh, Mike, to be honest with you,

312
00:21:25,251 --> 00:21:28,185
I'm going through a rough
time at work right now and...

313
00:21:31,724 --> 00:21:34,358
Well, if I change my
mind, I'll call you, okay?

314
00:21:34,426 --> 00:21:36,961
Are you still at
the Grand Hotel?

315
00:21:38,931 --> 00:21:41,531
Room 817.

316
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,400
Okay. Okay.

317
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:44,735
Bye.

318
00:22:05,558 --> 00:22:06,923
What'll it be?

319
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,725
Can I get a beer?

320
00:22:11,397 --> 00:22:13,330
$1.75.

321
00:22:16,135 --> 00:22:18,735
You know a woman
named Lisa Johnson?

322
00:22:18,804 --> 00:22:20,637
No.

323
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:22,786
Lives in an apartment
on Ashton and Third.

324
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,921
What are you asking me for?
That's halfway across town.

325
00:22:26,945 --> 00:22:28,225
She come in here?

326
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:29,780
That's what I heard.

327
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:32,282
No, don't know her.

328
00:22:35,988 --> 00:22:36,988
Yeah.

329
00:22:39,959 --> 00:22:41,792
Got a match?

330
00:22:47,066 --> 00:22:48,765
That's interesting.

331
00:22:48,834 --> 00:22:52,436
Not many people
light matches that way.

332
00:22:52,505 --> 00:22:55,272
Found this in an apartment
on Ashton and Third.

333
00:22:57,876 --> 00:22:59,054
I don't know what your story is,

334
00:22:59,078 --> 00:23:00,122
but you got something to say,

335
00:23:00,146 --> 00:23:01,386
why don't you just say it.

336
00:23:02,948 --> 00:23:05,015
Bye.

337
00:23:22,135 --> 00:23:23,033
Hello?

338
00:23:23,102 --> 00:23:24,568
Hi. How you doing?

339
00:23:24,637 --> 00:23:27,437
Oh... Ben.

340
00:23:27,506 --> 00:23:30,541
I did something today I've
never done before in my life.

341
00:23:30,609 --> 00:23:31,942
What?

342
00:23:32,011 --> 00:23:35,879
Well, I was supposed
to be at court at 10:30,

343
00:23:35,948 --> 00:23:37,514
and I forgot all about it.

344
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:39,450
Oh, I heard about that.

345
00:23:39,518 --> 00:23:40,417
You did?

346
00:23:40,485 --> 00:23:42,219
Yeah.

347
00:23:42,287 --> 00:23:44,755
You know how fast word
travels around the courthouse.

348
00:23:44,824 --> 00:23:46,189
Who told you?

349
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:47,191
Charlie.

350
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:49,893
The hot dog vendor?

351
00:23:49,962 --> 00:23:51,228
Yeah.

352
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:52,341
Hey, speaking of food...

353
00:23:52,365 --> 00:23:53,497
I'll cook.

354
00:23:53,565 --> 00:23:55,532
It's the least I can do.

355
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:57,579
I'll stop by the market
on my way home.

356
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:58,980
What market?
I'll meet you there.

357
00:23:59,004 --> 00:24:00,844
Oh, you don't have to do that.

358
00:24:00,906 --> 00:24:04,474
I just like to look at the
produce and push the cart.

359
00:24:04,543 --> 00:24:08,712
The Food Mart on Carson.

360
00:24:08,781 --> 00:24:10,147
Okay, I'll meet you there.

361
00:24:10,216 --> 00:24:12,416
And I'll get us a cart
that all the wheels work.

362
00:24:12,484 --> 00:24:14,044
Okay.

363
00:24:57,029 --> 00:24:58,406
Julie, it's okay. It's me.

364
00:24:58,430 --> 00:25:00,997
It's Nick Beloit!
He's right behind me!

365
00:25:12,144 --> 00:25:14,044
He got away. Oh!

366
00:25:14,113 --> 00:25:16,880
Julie, are you sure
it was Nick Beloit?

367
00:25:16,949 --> 00:25:18,215
Yes.

368
00:25:18,284 --> 00:25:20,262
Well, I didn't get a
look at his face, but...

369
00:25:20,286 --> 00:25:21,618
I just came from the bar

370
00:25:21,687 --> 00:25:23,865
he and his brother
own... He was working.

371
00:25:23,889 --> 00:25:26,790
There's no way that he could
have beaten me here. No way.

372
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:30,027
But if it wasn't Nick Beloit...

373
00:25:30,096 --> 00:25:32,496
who was it?

374
00:25:47,213 --> 00:25:48,645
This is good.

375
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:50,459
Yeah, I've had that a long time.

376
00:25:50,483 --> 00:25:53,350
All right, let's say it wasn't
Nick Beloit in that apartment.

377
00:25:53,419 --> 00:25:55,030
Could have been a friend of his.

378
00:25:55,054 --> 00:25:56,186
Maybe.

379
00:25:56,255 --> 00:25:58,200
Like the woman that
rented that apartment.

380
00:25:58,224 --> 00:26:00,090
It could have been a friend.

381
00:26:00,159 --> 00:26:03,060
Maybe... or maybe it has
nothing to do with Nick Beloit.

382
00:26:03,129 --> 00:26:06,030
You found the matchbook
with the matches folded down.

383
00:26:06,098 --> 00:26:08,198
Nick Beloit was
in that apartment.

384
00:26:09,868 --> 00:26:13,803
Or somebody who wanted
us to think it was Nick Beloit.

385
00:26:15,674 --> 00:26:18,409
Who... Who else was around

386
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:20,143
when he threatened you?

387
00:26:20,212 --> 00:26:21,645
Who<i> wasn't</i> around?

388
00:26:21,714 --> 00:26:22,846
The corridor was packed.

389
00:26:22,915 --> 00:26:24,315
Well, think back.

390
00:26:24,383 --> 00:26:26,784
Does anybody in
particular come to mind?

391
00:26:26,852 --> 00:26:29,953
You were there... Yeah.

392
00:26:30,022 --> 00:26:31,421
Eli...

393
00:26:31,490 --> 00:26:33,257
Harvey Goodman...

394
00:26:33,325 --> 00:26:35,692
that's Tom Beloit's lawyer...

395
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:39,596
And... Oh, there was this
friend of mine from Baltimore,

396
00:26:39,664 --> 00:26:40,931
Michael Eiseman.

397
00:26:40,999 --> 00:26:44,334
He, um, just showed
up out of the blue.

398
00:26:44,403 --> 00:26:47,137
And he said he was on
his way down to Florida.

399
00:26:47,206 --> 00:26:50,473
He called me yesterday.
He's still in town.

400
00:26:50,542 --> 00:26:53,510
But that's... that's
just a coincidence.

401
00:26:53,579 --> 00:26:55,212
He's a legal secretary.

402
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,624
We worked together in Baltimore.

403
00:26:56,648 --> 00:26:59,015
Oh... Oh, just-just a friend.

404
00:26:59,084 --> 00:27:02,419
I think he did ask me out once.

405
00:27:02,487 --> 00:27:04,399
Did you go? No.

406
00:27:04,423 --> 00:27:05,656
No, no.

407
00:27:05,724 --> 00:27:08,592
I remember I was very surprised

408
00:27:08,661 --> 00:27:12,295
because I never thought of
Mike as somebody I'd ever date.

409
00:27:12,364 --> 00:27:14,130
But I didn't go.

410
00:27:14,199 --> 00:27:15,632
And he never asked me again.

411
00:27:15,701 --> 00:27:17,334
Yeah...

412
00:27:17,402 --> 00:27:19,203
Yeah, well, uh...

413
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:24,942
Uh, I wonder if-if
we should, um...

414
00:27:25,010 --> 00:27:27,310
It can't be him.

415
00:27:27,379 --> 00:27:29,846
It just can't be.

416
00:27:39,958 --> 00:27:41,892
Julie...?

417
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:43,705
This is such a nice surprise.

418
00:27:43,729 --> 00:27:46,129
I thought you might've
gone back to Florida.

419
00:27:46,198 --> 00:27:47,698
Not yet.

420
00:27:47,766 --> 00:27:48,944
Something's bothering you.

421
00:27:48,968 --> 00:27:51,301
Why do you say that?

422
00:27:51,369 --> 00:27:52,503
I can tell.

423
00:27:52,571 --> 00:27:54,716
I-I used to watch
you a lot in the office,

424
00:27:54,740 --> 00:27:56,051
and I know when you're upset.

425
00:27:56,075 --> 00:27:58,708
Why did you watch me, Mike?

426
00:28:00,979 --> 00:28:02,545
You're pretty.

427
00:28:04,216 --> 00:28:05,815
Did I do something wrong?

428
00:28:05,884 --> 00:28:07,217
Are you mad at me?

429
00:28:07,286 --> 00:28:11,254
No, no, I'm not mad at you.

430
00:28:11,323 --> 00:28:13,924
But, uh...

431
00:28:13,992 --> 00:28:18,028
I do have a problem.

432
00:28:18,096 --> 00:28:22,132
Somebody... a man...

433
00:28:22,201 --> 00:28:25,235
Has been calling
me and following me.

434
00:28:27,239 --> 00:28:29,439
Oh, you think it's me?

435
00:28:29,508 --> 00:28:31,574
I don't know.

436
00:28:31,643 --> 00:28:36,547
Julie, I would never ever
do anything to upset you.

437
00:28:36,615 --> 00:28:38,148
Mike, I'm not accusing you.

438
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:39,282
It's just that...

439
00:28:41,486 --> 00:28:44,921
all of this started the
day you came to Atlanta.

440
00:28:44,990 --> 00:28:47,590
Oh.

441
00:28:47,659 --> 00:28:51,327
So you can understand
why I have to ask you.

442
00:28:53,365 --> 00:28:55,866
Why did you come to see me?

443
00:28:58,837 --> 00:29:02,071
I-I wanted to
take you to dinner,

444
00:29:02,140 --> 00:29:04,975
and... thank you.

445
00:29:05,043 --> 00:29:07,477
You... You helped me, years ago.

446
00:29:07,545 --> 00:29:10,180
Oh, Mike.

447
00:29:10,248 --> 00:29:12,883
I only treated you like
I treat everybody else.

448
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:15,352
No, you were always so nice.

449
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:17,932
I'm different; I'm... I'm shy.

450
00:29:17,956 --> 00:29:21,424
It's not easy for me to
make friends with women.

451
00:29:21,494 --> 00:29:23,293
And you were so nice.

452
00:29:23,362 --> 00:29:25,362
It meant a great deal to me.

453
00:29:27,566 --> 00:29:30,834
I don't know what to say.

454
00:29:30,903 --> 00:29:34,504
Well... I've made
friends with a lady.

455
00:29:34,573 --> 00:29:37,507
Um... she's shy, too.

456
00:29:37,576 --> 00:29:40,143
I don't know what to say.

457
00:29:40,212 --> 00:29:42,223
You don't have to say anything.

458
00:29:42,247 --> 00:29:44,481
You do believe me,
though, don't you?

459
00:29:47,219 --> 00:29:50,887
Yes, I believe you.

460
00:29:59,298 --> 00:30:00,763
Ben?

461
00:30:00,833 --> 00:30:02,743
Yeah, in here.

462
00:30:02,767 --> 00:30:04,545
Hey. Hey. She go see him?

463
00:30:04,569 --> 00:30:05,502
Yeah.

464
00:30:05,571 --> 00:30:06,847
It figures.

465
00:30:06,871 --> 00:30:08,049
Everything okay?
Did you stay close?

466
00:30:08,073 --> 00:30:09,073
Didn't have to.

467
00:30:09,108 --> 00:30:10,640
They never left the
lobby of the hotel.

468
00:30:10,709 --> 00:30:11,953
No? No.

469
00:30:11,977 --> 00:30:13,943
No, they talked a while,

470
00:30:14,012 --> 00:30:16,092
then she left, and he went
into the hotel restaurant,

471
00:30:16,148 --> 00:30:18,115
ate this big bowl of
cereal with sliced bananas

472
00:30:18,183 --> 00:30:19,682
and then went up to his room.

473
00:30:19,751 --> 00:30:20,828
In the middle of the afternoon?

474
00:30:20,852 --> 00:30:22,296
Yeah. I watched him
eat the whole bowl,

475
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:24,387
then watched him
go up to his room.

476
00:30:24,456 --> 00:30:27,023
Even listened for him to
snap that little security chain.

477
00:30:27,092 --> 00:30:29,126
What kind of bird is he?

478
00:30:29,194 --> 00:30:30,993
I don't know, he's
a little... little weird.

479
00:30:31,062 --> 00:30:32,095
He's average.

480
00:30:32,163 --> 00:30:33,463
Hmm.

481
00:30:33,532 --> 00:30:34,964
He could be the one.

482
00:30:35,033 --> 00:30:36,967
Could be. Yeah.

483
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:40,896
Well, this place is
clean as a whistle.

484
00:30:43,042 --> 00:30:45,208
Oh, uh... well,
what do you think?

485
00:30:45,277 --> 00:30:47,444
Whoever we're looking for,

486
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:49,813
he'd come in here...

487
00:30:49,882 --> 00:30:52,415
he'd sit there waiting
for Julie to come home,

488
00:30:52,484 --> 00:30:54,084
he'd use the phone to harass her

489
00:30:54,152 --> 00:30:56,152
and then he'd leave. Yep.

490
00:30:59,758 --> 00:31:02,626
One other thing he might've
done while he was waiting.

491
00:31:02,695 --> 00:31:04,628
What?

492
00:31:05,898 --> 00:31:07,864
What's that?

493
00:31:09,668 --> 00:31:12,002
When you drop a
phone book like that,

494
00:31:12,071 --> 00:31:15,271
it'll open up to the page
that's used the most.

495
00:31:15,340 --> 00:31:18,041
And I bet it opened up
to the restaurant section.

496
00:31:19,411 --> 00:31:20,243
Yeah.

497
00:31:20,312 --> 00:31:22,713
Any man...

498
00:31:22,781 --> 00:31:25,148
who waits for hours
has food delivered.

499
00:31:26,952 --> 00:31:28,284
You like pizza?

500
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:37,761
Hi.

501
00:31:41,199 --> 00:31:43,000
Julie?

502
00:31:44,937 --> 00:31:47,403
Julie, where are you?

503
00:31:47,472 --> 00:31:49,506
I'm in here. Oh.

504
00:31:52,044 --> 00:31:54,044
Boy!

505
00:31:54,113 --> 00:31:57,014
Somebody washed the curtains...

506
00:31:57,082 --> 00:31:58,548
the windows...

507
00:31:58,617 --> 00:31:59,549
and everything!

508
00:31:59,618 --> 00:32:00,884
I did.

509
00:32:00,953 --> 00:32:02,719
Why?

510
00:32:02,788 --> 00:32:04,721
Because everything was dirty.

511
00:32:04,790 --> 00:32:06,623
I just can't sit around
and do nothing.

512
00:32:06,692 --> 00:32:07,692
I'll go nuts.

513
00:32:16,134 --> 00:32:17,934
Uh...

514
00:32:18,002 --> 00:32:20,870
What if I took you to lunch?

515
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:24,541
I fixed some tuna
salad. It's in the fridge.

516
00:32:24,610 --> 00:32:28,845
Um, Julie, you've got to
stop cleaning that oven.

517
00:32:28,914 --> 00:32:31,014
I gotta keep busy.

518
00:32:33,552 --> 00:32:35,652
It's self-cleaning.

519
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:45,929
I knew that.

520
00:32:45,998 --> 00:32:46,830
Oh.

521
00:32:46,899 --> 00:32:47,964
Well, here, sit down

522
00:32:48,033 --> 00:32:49,710
and I'll fix you some lemonade.

523
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:53,570
Hello.

524
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:55,350
Let me talk to Julie.

525
00:32:55,374 --> 00:32:57,407
Who?

526
00:32:57,476 --> 00:32:58,942
Come on...

527
00:32:59,010 --> 00:33:00,255
You got the wrong number.

528
00:33:00,279 --> 00:33:02,312
I know she's there.

529
00:33:02,381 --> 00:33:04,147
Who are you?

530
00:33:04,216 --> 00:33:06,216
The pizza man.

531
00:33:06,285 --> 00:33:08,463
Well, listen, pizza man,
let me tell you something...

532
00:33:08,487 --> 00:33:10,031
You...!

533
00:33:10,055 --> 00:33:11,288
Damn.

534
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:13,823
The pizza man?

535
00:33:13,892 --> 00:33:16,326
That night he was looking
through your window,

536
00:33:16,395 --> 00:33:19,229
while he was waiting for you to
come home, he ordered a pizza.

537
00:33:19,297 --> 00:33:21,542
We went to a lot of places,

538
00:33:21,566 --> 00:33:23,778
but we never... never
found anybody who saw him.

539
00:33:23,802 --> 00:33:25,135
He was like "The Shadow."

540
00:33:25,203 --> 00:33:26,770
He knows I'm here.

541
00:33:26,839 --> 00:33:27,879
How did he find out?

542
00:33:27,906 --> 00:33:29,250
How? I don't know. I... I...

543
00:33:29,274 --> 00:33:31,141
I didn't tell anybody
I was staying here.

544
00:33:31,210 --> 00:33:33,120
Not a single soul. How
did he find out? I... I...

545
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:34,856
I don't know. Now he's
following both of us.

546
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:35,912
Here, sit down...

547
00:33:35,981 --> 00:33:37,447
I don't want to sit down!

548
00:33:37,516 --> 00:33:39,916
I want to get that guy!

549
00:33:39,985 --> 00:33:42,185
I want...

550
00:33:42,254 --> 00:33:45,789
I... I just want my life back.

551
00:33:45,857 --> 00:33:48,358
I know. I know.

552
00:33:48,427 --> 00:33:50,760
I know.

553
00:33:50,829 --> 00:33:53,363
Everything's gonna be all right.

554
00:33:57,735 --> 00:34:01,504
We've got to find
you another place...

555
00:34:01,573 --> 00:34:03,106
where you'll be safe.

556
00:34:07,179 --> 00:34:09,739
Doesn't Eli have a
place somewhere?

557
00:34:14,286 --> 00:34:16,846
Look, I don't know
what you're talking about.

558
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:21,624
Trespassing, harassment,
maybe even assault.

559
00:34:21,693 --> 00:34:24,105
Hey, if somebody is
harassing that broad,

560
00:34:24,129 --> 00:34:25,306
I say great.

561
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:26,629
More power to him.

562
00:34:26,698 --> 00:34:28,031
It isn't me.

563
00:34:28,100 --> 00:34:30,399
Well, if it isn't you,
somebody's doing his best

564
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:31,767
to make it look like you.

565
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:41,411
How many people know you
bend your matches over this way?

566
00:34:43,481 --> 00:34:45,441
Everybody who's
ever seen me smoke.

567
00:34:48,319 --> 00:34:50,565
After you threatened Julie
March at the courthouse,

568
00:34:50,589 --> 00:34:52,022
where'd you go?

569
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:56,526
Went home, changed
clothes, came straight here.

570
00:34:56,595 --> 00:35:00,196
Most of your customers regulars?

571
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:03,599
Yeah, yeah, except on weekends.

572
00:35:06,304 --> 00:35:08,471
The day your
brother was convicted,

573
00:35:08,540 --> 00:35:11,341
you remember seeing anybody
come in here you didn't know?

574
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:14,177
Not right off.

575
00:35:19,851 --> 00:35:22,519
Nah, I don't know; I don't know.

576
00:35:22,587 --> 00:35:28,592
I want you to come downtown
and look over some pictures.

577
00:35:28,660 --> 00:35:29,892
Here's the address.

578
00:35:32,196 --> 00:35:34,030
What kind of pictures?

579
00:35:34,098 --> 00:35:36,933
Oh, ex-cons, parolees,

580
00:35:37,002 --> 00:35:39,002
people who don't
like Julie March much.

581
00:35:39,070 --> 00:35:41,204
I could be there all day.

582
00:35:41,272 --> 00:35:43,306
You could be in
prison a lot longer.

583
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:45,007
9:00 a.m.

584
00:35:54,919 --> 00:35:56,453
This is so nice.

585
00:35:58,189 --> 00:36:01,157
Yeah. Yeah, it is, isn't it?

586
00:36:02,594 --> 00:36:04,271
You know, we
better head back in.

587
00:36:04,295 --> 00:36:06,140
It looks like we're
in for a storm.

588
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:07,275
Come on.

589
00:36:07,299 --> 00:36:09,365
Are you sure

590
00:36:09,434 --> 00:36:10,900
you don't need me back in town?

591
00:36:10,968 --> 00:36:12,547
I'm positive.

592
00:36:12,571 --> 00:36:14,704
Oh! I wish I could work,

593
00:36:14,772 --> 00:36:17,273
but all my files
are in the office.

594
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:19,520
Well, I can go back
into town tonight,

595
00:36:19,544 --> 00:36:21,589
pick up what you
need, and then bring it

596
00:36:21,613 --> 00:36:22,690
to you tomorrow... oh, boy.

597
00:36:22,714 --> 00:36:23,513
That would be great!

598
00:36:23,582 --> 00:36:26,216
Oh, thank you.

599
00:36:26,284 --> 00:36:28,551
And thank Paula, too,
for lending me your place.

600
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:29,552
That's okay. Come on!

601
00:36:29,621 --> 00:36:30,953
We're in for it! Let's go!

602
00:36:38,162 --> 00:36:39,273
Oh!

603
00:36:39,297 --> 00:36:42,198
Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh, I'm soaked!

604
00:36:42,266 --> 00:36:45,367
Check the, uh, dresser
in the bedroom upstairs.

605
00:36:45,436 --> 00:36:47,381
Paula may have left
some sweaters here, huh?

606
00:36:47,405 --> 00:36:48,504
It's freezing!

607
00:36:48,573 --> 00:36:51,140
I'll, uh, start a fire, huh?

608
00:37:27,945 --> 00:37:30,546
♪ ♪

609
00:37:59,811 --> 00:38:00,811
Hi.

610
00:38:06,150 --> 00:38:09,218
I... I found this in the drawer.

611
00:38:11,089 --> 00:38:13,890
Everything in here is about me.

612
00:38:16,595 --> 00:38:18,528
Yeah.

613
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:22,398
I think a lot of you, Julie.

614
00:38:37,749 --> 00:38:39,215
Where<i> is</i> Paula?

615
00:38:42,654 --> 00:38:43,986
Gone.

616
00:38:47,058 --> 00:38:48,691
I'm glad you're here.

617
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:51,927
Eli, you're very upset.

618
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:53,897
No, no, I'm not.

619
00:38:53,965 --> 00:38:55,398
I don't get upset, Julie.

620
00:38:55,466 --> 00:38:57,667
And besides, you're here now.

621
00:38:57,736 --> 00:39:01,203
You know, it took me quite
a while, but you are here.

622
00:39:01,272 --> 00:39:04,540
Isn't there somebody
you could talk to,

623
00:39:04,609 --> 00:39:06,976
like a doctor or a close friend?

624
00:39:07,044 --> 00:39:08,578
Somebody you could call...?

625
00:39:08,646 --> 00:39:10,112
I'll talk to you. No...

626
00:39:10,181 --> 00:39:12,915
No, this isn't right.

627
00:39:12,984 --> 00:39:15,118
Yes.

628
00:39:15,186 --> 00:39:18,754
Oh, yes, it is.

629
00:39:18,823 --> 00:39:21,657
Julie, you saw my scrapbook.

630
00:39:21,726 --> 00:39:24,426
You don't know how often

631
00:39:24,495 --> 00:39:25,906
I have dreamed
of having you here.

632
00:39:25,930 --> 00:39:30,033
It is going to be so
wonderful now, Julie.

633
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:32,468
It's just...

634
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:34,570
the two of us together.

635
00:39:36,408 --> 00:39:37,440
You and me...

636
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:39,990
so close...

637
00:39:41,679 --> 00:39:42,679
touching.

638
00:39:46,818 --> 00:39:48,684
You and me, Julie.

639
00:39:48,753 --> 00:39:50,686
Just you and me.

640
00:39:50,755 --> 00:39:52,388
I have to go.

641
00:39:52,456 --> 00:39:54,257
Don't you understand?

642
00:39:54,325 --> 00:39:56,659
I think about you all the time.

643
00:39:56,728 --> 00:39:58,639
Eli, we can talk about
this another time.

644
00:39:58,663 --> 00:39:59,743
No!

645
00:40:03,301 --> 00:40:05,535
You're going to stay.

646
00:40:05,603 --> 00:40:06,869
You want to.

647
00:40:06,938 --> 00:40:08,838
I have to go.

648
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:11,586
Ow!

649
00:40:11,610 --> 00:40:12,808
Oh!

650
00:40:13,912 --> 00:40:15,678
You're staying.

651
00:41:11,569 --> 00:41:12,601
Oh!

652
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:16,372
You are not going to leave me.

653
00:41:16,441 --> 00:41:19,075
You're here. You are here.

654
00:41:19,144 --> 00:41:20,309
Do you understand me, hmm?

655
00:41:20,378 --> 00:41:22,938
Yes, yes...

656
00:41:25,816 --> 00:41:27,316
Don't make me angry.

657
00:41:30,088 --> 00:41:33,889
Don't... do that, hmm?

658
00:41:33,958 --> 00:41:35,724
No, no, no.

659
00:41:41,633 --> 00:41:44,800
What about this guy?

660
00:41:44,869 --> 00:41:47,348
Do you recognize this guy?

661
00:41:47,372 --> 00:41:48,671
Uh...

662
00:41:52,177 --> 00:41:55,010
Well... this guy?

663
00:41:57,115 --> 00:41:58,180
Here you go.

664
00:41:58,249 --> 00:41:59,249
Uh, nope.

665
00:41:59,316 --> 00:42:00,436
Fresh from the photo lab.

666
00:42:00,484 --> 00:42:01,561
Oh, good, good, good, good.

667
00:42:01,585 --> 00:42:02,963
Take a look at this guy.

668
00:42:02,987 --> 00:42:05,588
You recognize him?

669
00:42:07,291 --> 00:42:08,224
Nope.

670
00:42:08,292 --> 00:42:09,324
You sure?

671
00:42:11,228 --> 00:42:12,495
Yep.

672
00:42:16,567 --> 00:42:17,634
Have you spoken to Julie?

673
00:42:17,702 --> 00:42:20,269
I tried to call and
the phone was busy.

674
00:42:20,338 --> 00:42:22,639
This guy looks familiar.

675
00:42:28,146 --> 00:42:30,157
That's Eli Boward.

676
00:42:30,181 --> 00:42:31,391
He works with Julie.

677
00:42:31,415 --> 00:42:34,917
She was with him
outside the courtroom.

678
00:42:34,986 --> 00:42:35,884
She was?

679
00:42:35,954 --> 00:42:37,234
Well, so was I.

680
00:42:39,523 --> 00:42:41,324
I was so mad, all I
remember seeing is her.

681
00:42:41,392 --> 00:42:43,503
Well, well, come over here.

682
00:42:43,527 --> 00:42:45,328
Come over here.

683
00:42:47,365 --> 00:42:49,498
Try this guy.

684
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:52,127
What about this guy?

685
00:42:58,643 --> 00:43:01,310
I'm telling you, I've
seen that guy before,

686
00:43:01,378 --> 00:43:03,679
and it wasn't in that
courtroom either.

687
00:43:09,687 --> 00:43:10,752
Napoleon brandy.

688
00:43:10,821 --> 00:43:13,155
This guy came in my
place three nights in a row,

689
00:43:13,224 --> 00:43:15,469
sat down at the end of the
bar drinking Napoleon brandy.

690
00:43:15,493 --> 00:43:17,259
Are you sure?

691
00:43:17,328 --> 00:43:22,531
I finally remember, now
you don't believe me?

692
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,166
You got, you got
gas in your car?

693
00:43:24,235 --> 00:43:26,402
Enough to get us there.

694
00:43:38,249 --> 00:43:40,483
Don't try to run away again.

695
00:43:40,552 --> 00:43:42,484
Don't do that.

696
00:43:47,591 --> 00:43:51,360
You see, I don't understand.

697
00:43:51,429 --> 00:43:53,040
I thought if I
brought you up here,

698
00:43:53,064 --> 00:43:54,663
you would want to be here,

699
00:43:54,732 --> 00:43:56,866
you would want to
be with me all the way.

700
00:43:58,669 --> 00:43:59,680
Well, you will, you will.

701
00:43:59,704 --> 00:44:01,871
Right. You will, you will.

702
00:44:01,940 --> 00:44:04,473
It just takes some people
longer than others, that's all.

703
00:44:04,542 --> 00:44:05,775
I mean, I can wait.

704
00:44:05,844 --> 00:44:07,210
I can be patient.

705
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:11,360
But, of course, you
already knew that, huh?

706
00:44:17,188 --> 00:44:20,623
You are going to
want to be with me.

707
00:44:22,727 --> 00:44:24,026
It'll be good.

708
00:44:24,095 --> 00:44:26,062
It'll be good.

709
00:44:30,401 --> 00:44:31,801
Don't.

710
00:44:34,472 --> 00:44:35,938
Now, don't...

711
00:44:43,213 --> 00:44:45,548
Eli?

712
00:44:45,617 --> 00:44:46,748
Ben Matlock.

713
00:44:51,889 --> 00:44:55,124
Eli, what's going on?!

714
00:44:55,193 --> 00:44:57,760
Well, you already know, Ben.

715
00:44:57,829 --> 00:44:59,828
Get back in your car.

716
00:44:59,897 --> 00:45:01,063
Aw, come on, Eli.

717
00:45:01,132 --> 00:45:03,198
Just let me talk
with you for a minute.

718
00:45:03,267 --> 00:45:06,535
No, get back in your car, Ben.

719
00:45:06,604 --> 00:45:09,005
Eli, you don't want
to hurt anybody.

720
00:45:11,075 --> 00:45:13,075
Get out of here!

721
00:45:13,144 --> 00:45:14,810
There'll be other people coming.

722
00:45:14,879 --> 00:45:16,879
You can't run 'em all off.

723
00:45:24,055 --> 00:45:26,615
Julie!

724
00:45:40,405 --> 00:45:42,838
Well, I'll be damned... Eli.

725
00:45:43,942 --> 00:45:45,741
You never know, do you?

726
00:45:45,810 --> 00:45:47,910
I'll call the police.

727
00:45:47,979 --> 00:45:49,645
Yeah.

728
00:45:55,352 --> 00:45:56,430
You all right?

729
00:45:56,454 --> 00:45:58,855
I don't know.

730
00:46:01,258 --> 00:46:02,538
You look good, anyway.

731
00:46:04,896 --> 00:46:06,495
Let's go home.

732
00:46:06,563 --> 00:46:09,198
Let's do that.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
